---
// Getting started: the Docs landing (header "Docs" lands here). What Facet is, what you need, and the path through the
// docs: install -> Home Assistant -> screens -> AI screens -> reference -> roadmap. Released features only.
import Docs, { type Heading } from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
import { url } from '../../lib/nav';
import { screenById, screenHref } from '../../lib/data';

const home = screenById('home');
const headings: Heading[] = [
  { depth: 2, slug: 'need', text: 'What you need' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'install', text: '1. Install Facet' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'home-assistant', text: '2. Connect to Home Assistant' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'screens', text: '3. Find your way round' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'ai', text: '4. Make your own screens' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'reference', text: '5. Go deeper' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'contribute', text: '6. Help make Facet better' },
];
---

<Docs edit="site/src/pages/docs/index.astro" title="Getting started" description="What Facet is, what you need, and the steps from a blank panel to your own screens." group="Start here" current={url('/docs/')} headings={headings}>
  <p class="lede">
    Facet turns a small touch screen on the wall into a panel for your home. It runs on ESP32 panels with ESPHome,
    talks to Home Assistant, and every screen is built from one design system, so it all looks and feels the same.
  </p>

  <div class="callout">
    <span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <p>Facet is early. The firmware is a preview build, and new screens arrive often: the <a href={url('/roadmap/')}>roadmap</a> shows what is available and what is next.</p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="need">What you need</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      A supported panel: the <strong>Waveshare ESP32-P4-86</strong> (4 inch, 720 x 720) or the
      <strong>Guition ESP32-S3-4848S040</strong> (4 inch, 480 x 480). Both fit a standard wall box.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Home Assistant</strong> with the ESPHome integration (it is built in).</li>
    <li>A computer with Chrome or Edge and a USB-C data cable, for the first install.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="install">1. Install Facet</h2>
  <p>
    Flash the firmware from your browser on the <a href={url('/install/')}>Install</a> page, then put the panel on your
    Wi-Fi. It takes a few minutes and needs no other tools.
  </p>

  <h2 id="home-assistant">2. Connect to Home Assistant</h2>
  <p>
    Home Assistant finds the panel on your network. Add it, then allow it to perform Home Assistant actions so its
    controls can switch your lights and more. The steps are on the <a href={url('/install/#home-assistant')}>Install</a> page.
    Firmware updates then arrive in Home Assistant too. Something not working? See
    <a href={url('/docs/troubleshooting/')}>Updating and troubleshooting</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="screens">3. Find your way round</h2>
  <p>
    The panel starts on {home ? <a href={screenHref(home)}>Home</a> : 'Home'}: your cards at a glance, with the other
    screens a tap away. Lights, covers, media, weather, the clock, timers, the calendar and energy each have a screen.
    <a href={url('/screens/')}>Screens</a> shows every one live, with what it shows, its settings and where its data comes from.
    <a href={url('/docs/home-cards/')}>Home cards</a> explains the card sizes and how to choose what is on Home.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">4. Make your own screens</h2>
  <p>
    Want something Facet does not have? Describe it to an AI assistant and it builds the screen from Facet's own
    components. <a href={url('/ai/')}>Make screens with AI</a> has the rules, a starter prompt and how to send the
    result to your panel.
  </p>

  <h2 id="reference">5. Go deeper</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href={url('/docs/concepts/components/')}>Concepts</a>: how components, design tokens and <a href={url('/docs/concepts/firmware/')}>the firmware</a> fit together.</li>
    <li><a href={url('/components/')}>Components</a>: every building block, drawn live by the panel renderer.</li>
    <li><a href={url('/foundations/')}>Design system</a>: the colour, type, space, motion, icons and sound every screen is made from.</li>
    <li><a href={url('/docs/faq/')}>FAQ and hardware</a>: the supported panels and the questions people ask first.</li>
    <li><a href={url('/roadmap/')}>Roadmap</a>: where Facet is headed, area by area.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="contribute">6. Help make Facet better</h2>
  <p>
    Facet gets better with every person who tries it. Tell us what broke, test it on your panel, fix a line in these
    docs or write some code: <a href={url('/contributing/')}>Contributing</a> has every way in, and most need no code.
  </p>
</Docs>
